diate"><addressbook><name>NAKATA, YUKIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGITA, NAOKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATTA YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATA YUKIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGITA NAOKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATTA, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATA, YUKIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGITA, NAOKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p> A Petri dish (S) storing therein a culture medium (K) with a specified thickness is supported on the dish support (17) of a casing (14) and then a nozzle holding member (13) is fitted to the upper portion of the casing (14).  When a motor (19) is driven to rotate a high static pressure fan (18), air introduced through the hole (12a) of a nozzle (15) flows through the space between the nozzle (15) and the medium (K); a high trapping efficiency can be then maintained with the distance between the medium and the nozzle set to 0.5 to 1.5 mm.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une boîte de Pétri (S) stockant un milieu de culture (K) d'une épaisseur spécifiée, prenant appui sur le support de boîte (17) d'un boîtier (14), un élément porte-buse (13) étant ajusté sur la partie supérieure dudit boîtier (14). Lorsqu'un moteur (19) fait tourner un ventilateur (18) à pression statique élevée, l'air introduit par l'alésage (12a) de la buse (15) s'écoule dans l'espace situé entre la buse (15) et le milieu (K). Il est ainsi possible de maintenir une efficacité de piégeage élevée, la distance entre la buse et le milieu se situant entre 0,5 et 1,5mm.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>